1
00:04:05,806 --> 00:04:11,806
Sometimes the last person on earth you want to be with
is the one person you can't be without.

2
00:08:11,612 --> 00:08:17,612
Pride & Prejudice is a drama, romance film directed by Joe Wright.

3
00:12:17,419 --> 00:12:23,419
A story of love and life among the landed English
gentry during the Georgian era.

4
00:16:23,225 --> 00:16:29,225
Bennet is a gentleman living in Hertfordshire with his overbearing wife and five daughters, but if he dies their house will be inherited by a distant
cousin whom they have never met, so the family's future happiness and security is dependent on the daughters making good marriages.

5
00:20:29,032 --> 00:20:35,032
Elizabeth Bennet, played by Keira Knightley.

6
00:24:34,838 --> 00:24:40,838
Mr. Darcy, played by Matthew Macfadyen.

7
00:28:40,645 --> 00:28:46,645
Mrs. Bennet, played by Brenda Blethyn.

8
00:32:46,451 --> 00:32:52,451
Jane Bennet, played by Rosamund Pike.

9
00:36:52,258 --> 00:36:58,258
Kitty Bennet, played by Carey Mulligan.

10
00:40:58,064 --> 00:41:04,064
Lydia Bennet, played by Jena Malone.

11
00:45:03,870 --> 00:45:09,870
Pride & Prejudice is a 2005 period romance film directed by Joe Wright, in his feature
directorial debut, based on Jane Austen's 1813 novel of the same name.

12
00:49:09,677 --> 00:49:15,677
The film features five sisters from an English family of landed gentry as they
deal with issues of marriage, morality, and misconceptions.

13
00:53:15,483 --> 00:53:21,483
Keira Knightley stars as Elizabeth Bennet, while Matthew
Macfadyen plays Mr Darcy, who falls in love with her.

14
00:57:21,290 --> 00:57:27,290
Screenwriter Deborah Moggach initially attempted to make her script as faithful to the novel as
possible, writing from Elizabeth's perspective while preserving much of the original dialogue.

15
01:01:27,096 --> 01:01:33,096
Wright encouraged greater deviation from the text,
including changing the Bennet family dynamics.

16
01:05:32,903 --> 01:05:38,903
Wright and Moggach set the film in an earlier period and avoided depicting a "perfectly
clean Regency world", presenting instead a "muddy hem version" of the time.

17
01:09:38,709 --> 01:09:44,709
It was shot entirely on location in England on an 11-week schedule.

18
01:13:44,516 --> 01:13:50,516
Wright found casting difficult due to past
performances of particular characters.

19
01:17:50,322 --> 01:17:56,322
The filmmakers had to balance who they thought was best for
each role with the studio's desire for stars.

20
01:21:56,129 --> 01:22:02,129
Knightley was well known in part from her role in the Pirates of the Caribbean
film series, while Macfadyen had no international name recognition.

21
01:26:01,935 --> 01:26:07,935
Produced by Working Title Films in association with StudioCanal, Pride & Prejudice was released on
16 September 2005 in the United Kingdom and on 11 November in the United States.

22
01:30:07,741 --> 01:30:13,741
The film's themes emphasise realism, romanticism and family.

23
01:34:13,548 --> 01:34:19,548
It was marketed to a younger, mainstream audience; promotional items noted that it came from the producers of
2001's romantic comedy Bridget Jones's Diary before acknowledging its provenance as an Austen novel.

24
01:38:19,354 --> 01:38:25,354
Austen scholars opined that Wright's work created a new hybrid genre by blending
traditional traits of the heritage film with "youth-oriented filmmaking techniques".

25
01:42:25,161 --> 01:42:31,161
Pride & Prejudice was successful at the box office, grossing
$121.6 million worldwide on a $28 million budget.

26
01:46:30,967 --> 01:46:36,967
It received positive reviews from critics, with
praise for Knightley's performance.

27
01:50:36,774 --> 01:50:42,774
It received four nominations at the 78th Academy Awards, including Best Actress for the
20-year-old Knightley, making her the third-youngest Best Actress nominee at the time.

28
01:54:42,580 --> 01:54:48,580
The film received other accolades, including the BAFTA Award for Outstanding
Debut by a British Writer, Director or Producer for Wright.

29
01:58:48,387 --> 01:58:54,387
The film explores themes of based on novel or book,
england, bachelor, family relationships, suitor.

30
02:02:54,193 --> 02:03:00,193
The tone is emotional.
